   ],
   "description": "TMPAVG: the layer-average temperature with the profile clipped at the freezing point t0. Eight branches over the orderings of the upper-boundary, mid-layer and lower-boundary temperatures about t0. Where the whole layer is on one side of t0 the result is the ordinary weighted average (tu + 2 tm + td)/4; where the layer straddles t0 the sub-freezing portion is located by linear interpolation (the x0/xup/xdn lengths) and the rest of the layer contributes t0 rather than its own temperature. That clipping is what holds a partly frozen layer on the melting plateau.",
